WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.610
If you're looking for an affordable bicycle
that's durable and has great shock absorption

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.060
capabilities, then a bike made of steel is
for you.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:13.710
It's a bit heavier than a high end bicycle
made of aluminum or carbon fiber.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:19.110
But this rugged material buys you a smoother
ride at a significantly lower price.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.450
There's three speed steel bicycle is sturdy
and comfortable enough to ride recreationally

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.490
or daily to school or work.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.860
A cargo rack in the rear can hold your
purse, backpack or briefcase.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.300
The bike is made of Chromoly steel, which is
pound for pound stronger than standard steel.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.180
To prepare the bike's tubular parts,
including the frame, a worker cut steel tube

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.080
with a horizontal bandsaw into specific
length pieces.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:59.500
He then clamped certain frame pieces into a
milling machine which will cut a curve into

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.880
one or both ends, depending on the piece's
location in the final assembly.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.460
This notch, as it's called, will let the
tube butt up against the side of an adjacent

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.980
tube when the bike's frame is assembled.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.740
The notched edge is ragged, so the worker
smooths it out with a small belt sander.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.640
Certain frame parts are straight.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.400
Others bend to make the bent ones.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:34.770
Another worker places the piece of tube in a
tube bender, a press that forces the tube

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.270
against a curved die.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.960
Once all the frame parts are ready, a welder
clamps them in a fixture which correctly

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.790
positions them for assembly.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.400
He works with a welding torch in one hand and
a rod of filler metal in the other.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:02:00.190
The torch melts adjacent tubes at their
meeting point so that they fuse together.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:05.290
The welder also melts in some filler metal
to strengthen the joint.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:17.470
The bicycle frame is made up of nine major
parts.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:26.580
And the welder welds them to each other in
two sections, forming the rear triangle and

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.900
the front triangle.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:32.820
This is the rear one, which alone requires
nine meticulous welds.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.940
Once each triangle is separately assembled,
he welds them together.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:50.970
Another worker sprays the frame with powder
coat primer, then color.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:57.630
Powder coat is an industrial grade paint
like finish, which he bakes onto the metal at

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.810
almost 400°F for 20 minutes.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.510
When the frame comes out of the oven,
another worker presses steel caps into what's

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.710
called the head tube.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:16.840
That vertical tube at the front of the
frame, which holds the handlebars on top and

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.620
the fork for the front wheel at the bottom,
bearings inside the caps.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.250
Let the handlebars and fork turn left and
right with ease.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.130
To put the bicycle together.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:34.140
The worker suspends the frame in an assembly
stand and then inserts the bottom bracket,

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.440
which will ultimately support the bike's
drivetrain system.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.930
The bike's fenders are made of sheet steel
that shaped with pressure applying rollers.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:49.350
The rear fender attaches to the rear dropout
and defender mounts at two other locations on

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.880
the frame's rear triangle.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:57.410
He screws the cargo rack to middle and rear
rack supports.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:01.930
Then he inserts and bolts the rear wheel
into the rear dropout.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.660
The wheel hub has three built in gears.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:09.130
The hub and rim are made of aluminum, which
is lightweight and doesn't rust.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.130
The wheel spokes are stainless steel.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.520
Next, the worker installs the drivetrain
system.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:21.550
Inserting the crank arms already mounted to
the chain ring onto the bottom bracket.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.580
He tightens the bolts securely with a torque
wrench.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:33.120
Workers, then insert the fork into the
bottom of the head tube and chrome plated

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.280
steel handlebars into the top mount.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.440
The front fender and front wheel.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.030
Then install the pedals.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:45.240
Vinyl, seat chain and chain guard with the
gear shifter and front brake lever on the

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:49.590
handlebars. This steel bicycle is ready to
hit the road.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:56.100
For some pet owners, feeding raw food to
Fido is a natural choice.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:01.260
It harkens back to the common ancestor of
all dog breeds, the wolf in the wild.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.780
Wolves eat raw meat and occasionally some
greens.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:10.290
So the theory goes that dogs are genetically
predisposed to thrive on a raw meat diet.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:18.010
Dogs have been domesticated for thousands of
years, but when it comes to their diet, they

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.780
can still go a little wild.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:25.210
Raw canine cuisine may be a foreign concept
to some pet owners, but it's becoming more

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:31.780
mainstream. The makers of raw dog food often
mix fruits and vegetables with meat to

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.540
provide fiber and create a balanced meal.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.770
The process starts with a lot of slicing and
dicing.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:46.040
A food worker chops the fruits and veggies
into smaller pieces so they'll be able to go

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.870
through a grinder more easily.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:56.310
He also removes the seeds from the apples in
the squash because the seeds aren't as easily

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:00.420
digested as the rest of the fruit and
provide no additional nutrition.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:10.510
This raw pet food recipe calls for a variety
of fruits and vegetables, though in total,

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:13.270
they will comprise just 5% of the meal.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:19.330
The rest of the raw blend will consist of
meat, bones, organs and fish.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:28.190
Another food worker chops up the chicken,
which has been organically raised and has

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:30.620
even been approved for human consumption.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:33.860
Except for the breasts.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:37.220
All the parts of the chicken will be used in
the main recipe.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:41.420
This includes the heart, liver, gizzards and
the bones.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:50.890
Raul. Whole sardines, anchovies and mackerel
will add essential fatty acids to the Raul

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:59.280
Chicken blend. All the ingredients have been
prepared and are now ready for grinding.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:05.520
A worker feeds the components to the grinder
in small batches, interspersing the meat,

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.290
fish and the vegetables.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:17.070
This ensures even distribution as the
Grinder minces everything to a uniform

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.300
particle size.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:27.230
The result is a thick emulsion of finely
ground chicken, meat, bones, vegetables,

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:28.550
fruits and fish.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.670
She transfers the minced raw ingredients to a
mixer.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.230
The revolving paddles further blend the
food.

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:49.240
After about five minutes in the mixer, all
the ingredients have been combined into one

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:50.980
homogeneous raw mass.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:56.410
This chicken blend is now complete.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:01.150
The worker divides it into £5 batches and
scoops it into bags.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:07.650
She vacuum seals the bag.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:14.940
Removing all the air inside will allow the
raw blend to stay fresh longer, refrigerated.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:17.040
It should last for up to ten days.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.340
And if frozen, it should be good for several
months.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.150
For the furry members of the family.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.280
Dinner is ready to be served.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:31.410
To make some raw pet snacks.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:36.810
A worker decals New Zealand green lipped
mussels, a species that is believed to have

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.990
fast acting anti-inflammatory properties.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:46.520
After she cuts the muscles free from the
shells, she places them on racks for air

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:55.700
drying. She transfers the rack into a drying
tent where fans keep air circulating 24 hours

00:08:55.730 --> 00:09:00.680
a day. As the muscles dry, they shrink.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:06.740
After 72 hours in the tent, the moisture
content is substantially reduced.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:12.910
Air drying has preserved the flesh of the
mussels in the raw state while preventing

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.430
damage to the nutrients and enzymes they
contain.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.770
Now preserved.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:25.380
She packs the muscles into plastic bags and
adds an iron oxide packet to absorb oxygen

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.030
and prevent spoilage.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:33.870
This raw pet food is now ready to nourish
the wolf in your dog.

